# pico_epaper_b

A Raspberry Pi Pico with a Waveshare Pico-ePaper-2.66-B attached directly to
its headers. The board inherits the Pico ARM SDK platform and fixes a 152 by
296 native-orientation black, white, and red panel on SPI1.

The carrier uses the same GP11 DIN, GP10 CLK, GP9 CS, GP8 DC, GP12 reset, and
GP13 busy wiring as the monochrome Pico-ePaper-2.66. Selection is explicit
because the carrier exposes no readable panel identity signal.

https://www.waveshare.com/wiki/Pico-ePaper-2.66-B
